course: dictionary
lesson: 15030
title: Words that hold back
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one to use. «Restraint» is one of them. Read the sentence around it, then ask: is this about a thing, or about how a person behaves?
explain: «The car seat has a strong restraint that keeps the child safe.» Here a restraint is a thing, like a strap or belt, that holds someone back from moving.
explain: «Mia showed restraint and did not shout back when her brother teased her.» Here restraint is calm control of your feelings or actions. Mia did not let her anger take over.
explain: «The club has a restraint on how many games each team can play.» Here a restraint is a rule or limit. Each team has a set boundary, so the word means a rule.
fact: Restraint means something that holds a person or thing back, or calm control of your feelings and actions.
fact: «Child restraint» is the official name for a car seat that keeps a child safe.
fact: «Show restraint» means staying calm and not reacting in anger.
fact: «Without restraint» means with no limit or control, as in «She laughed without restraint».
fact: Restraint can name a thing, a behaviour, or a rule, so check the context to find which one.
exercise: «The child restraint in the back seat kept her safe.» What is a child restraint? | A sweet treat for the car ride | A long journey in the car | *A car seat that keeps a child safe
exercise: «Tom showed restraint when his friend broke his pencil and did not shout.» What does showed restraint mean? | *Stayed calm and did not react in anger | Broke another pencil too | Ran out of the classroom | Shouted as loudly as he could
exercise: «The club has a restraint on how many games each team can play.» What is a restraint here? | A happy feeling | *A rule or limit | A loud noise | A seat belt
test: «The strap across her chest was a restraint that held her in her seat.» What is a restraint here? | A calm feeling | A bright colour | *Something that holds a person back | A sweet snack
test: «He ate the cake without restraint, and finished the whole plate.» What does without restraint mean? | With a fork and a plate | With careful, calm control | Slowly and politely | *With no limit or control
exam: «She spoke with restraint when the crowd began to shout.» What does restraint mean here? | A rule about how long she could speak | A loud and angry voice | A rope tied around her hands | *Calm control of her feelings and actions
